    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-2604",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14131901/assets/867b3664e93f42c55a2f97dc28bf66794484e226981632c85f725926cec77def.png)\n\nWhat type of angle is $\\angle RST,$ shown in the figure above?",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that the vertex of $\\angle RST$ is point $S,$ not point $T.$ So $\\angle RST$ is *not* a straight angle.\n\nAs a result, the two rays $\\overset{\\longrightarrow}{SR}$ and $\\overset{\\longrightarrow}{ST}$ of our angle coincide. So, we can think of $\\angle RST$ as:\n\n- A *null* angle, assuming it doesn't turn at all.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14131901/assets/a8916a724d4463bf2047c919b73770160d3124838b61af0dcdc2b9e04322381a.png)\n\n- A *full* angle, assuming it makes one full turn.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14131901/assets/9cd768b4361e95a18ffa52d6315fb5ea6cd0cf6784bc4c9e12b1bae1f6566755.png)\n\nSo, the answer is \"Null\" or \"Full.\"",
